{"lc": 1, "type": "constructor", "id": ["langchain", "schema", "document", "Document"], "kwargs": {"metadata": {"thread_id": "2707038_2707036", "turn_ids": ["2707038_2707036", "2707037_2707039", "2707040_2707041"], "root_turns": ["2707038_2707036"]}, "page_content": "Customer: text: Hi @SpotifyCares If there are a load of old albums by UK artists that were only released in the UK which @79397 and @35937 have uploaded to you but have geoblocked in the UK what can you do? The labels are refusing to help and we\u2019re deprived of amazing pop! Help please!\nAgent: text: @760238 Hi Rob! We\u2019d love to have all music available, but we have some info about content here: https://t.co/0i8GpimuDa /BE\n  Customer: text: @SpotifyCares Thanks but you haven\u2019t read my tweet and jumped straight into stock answer mode. The labels have put albums online intended for the UK market and then blocked them in the country they are intended for. You\u2019ve gotta admit that seems odd?\n  Agent: text: @760238 We understand where you're coming from. Licensing agreements affect content availability. Hopefully we'll have it available to you in the future /RS\n    Customer: text: @SpotifyCares I don\u2019t think you do. Why would a UK label upload an album for the UK market and then block in the UK if there was a licensing issue? It\u2019s clearly errors. Alisha\u2019s Attic\u2019s 1st&amp;3rd albums are on but the 2nd is on but blocked. All the same label. Can\u2019t be a licensing issue! Thanks.\n    Agent: text: @760238 We do our best! But since agreements are sometimes ongoing, or can't be reached with the content provider, region restrictions are applied. Fingers crossed we'll be able to have it soon /LS", "type": "Document"}}